  "names": {
   "summary": "A 72-byte beacon with several small-integer bytes at the start, then multi-byte fields at 15-35 that look like float or GNSS-style data. Many fields are partly decoded: some track eclipse state only through coarse coupling, and the multi-byte ones look like misaligned floats. Evidence is weak overall.",
   "fields": [
    {
     "offset": 2,
     "name": "unknown_byte_2",
     "category": "unknown",
     "unit": "raw",
     "scale": "raw",
     "confidence": 0.1,
     "rationale": "The median is constant at 70 in both sun and shadow, with 10 distinct values and a weak lag correlation (-0.5). The correlation comes from outlier frames, not a physical response. It co-moves with offsets 3 and 4, so it may be a status or mode field. [3/3 samples agree]"
    },
    {
     "offset": 3,
     "name": "unknown_byte_3",
     "category": "unknown",
     "unit": "raw",
     "scale": "raw",
     "confidence": 0.1,
     "rationale": "The median is a constant 5 in all regimes and the value is mostly static. The weak orbit R2 of 0.27 is not enough to claim a physical meaning. It co-moves with offsets 2 and 4, so it is probably part of the same status group. [3/3 samples agree]"
    },
    {
     "offset": 4,
     "name": "unknown_signed_byte_4",
     "category": "unknown",
     "unit": "raw",
     "scale": "raw",
     "confidence": 0.1,
     "rationale": "The median is constant at -67 in every regime. The lag correlation of 0.47 is driven by occasional outliers and it moves with offsets 2 and 3. It looks like a mode or status byte. [3/3 samples agree]"
    },
    {
     "offset": 15,
     "name": "unknown_u24_15",
     "category": "unknown",
     "unit": "raw",
     "scale": "raw",
     "confidence": 0.133,
     "rationale": "The values are near 13.2M in shadow and 4.8M in sun, and the range runs up to 0xFFFFFF. That looks like misaligned multi-byte data or a float. Its sun correlation may reflect a pass-dependent artefact, not a physical quantity. [3/3 samples agree]"
    },
    {
     "offset": 21,
     "name": "unknown_signed_byte_21",
     "category": "unknown",
     "unit": "raw",
     "scale": "raw",
     "confidence": 0.15,
     "rationale": "It is higher in shadow (median 74) than in sun (-54 to 0), has only 8 distinct values and shows a rising step profile in sun. That could be a coarse sun-linked quantity, but it is not attributable to any specific sensor. [3/3 samples agree]"
    },
    {
     "offset": 22,
     "name": "gnss_position_eci_z",
     "category": "navigation",
     "unit": "m",
     "scale": "raw / 992.18 km, so about raw * 1.0 m; approx. metres",
     "confidence": 0.317,
     "rationale": "The float matches the ECI z position in 36% of frames with a scale near 1000 per km, which points to metres. The remaining frames hold stale or garbage values (min -1e13), so confidence is moderate. [3/3 samples agree]"
    },
    {
     "offset": 27,
     "name": "unknown_s24_27",
     "category": "unknown",
     "unit": "raw",
     "scale": "raw",
     "confidence": 0.1,
     "rationale": "Weak orbit correlation (R2 0.32) and a wide signed range of about \u00b15M. It could be a GNSS-like value or misaligned float bytes, but the evidence is insufficient to say. [3/3 samples agree]"
    },
    {
     "offset": 32,
     "name": "unknown_u16_32",
     "category": "unknown",
     "unit": "raw",
     "scale": "raw",
     "confidence": 0.1,
     "rationale": "The median stays near 17800 in every regime, with extremes at 0 and about 50000. It looks like a float fragment or a sentinel value. [3/3 samples agree]"
    },
